  "status": "Application Under Consideration",
  "description": "The proposal seeks planning permission for the conversion of the existing detached garage (approximately 23sqm) together with the erection of a modest single-storey rear linked extension within the residential curtilage.\n\nThe development will provide ancillary living accommodation incidental to the main dwellinghouse. The structure will retain the existing ridge height of approximately 2.9 metres and remain subordinate in scale and appearance to the host property.\n\nThe proposal preserves a substantial proportion of the rear garden, with approximately 18 metres (around 73%) of private amenity space remaining. The development does not create a separate dwelling, does not introduce independent access, and will remain functionally and physically integrated with the main residence.\n\nThe site is located within Flood Zone 3 \n\nflood-map-planning-2026-02-27T1…\n\n, and appropriate flood mitigation measures will be incorporated to ensure the development is safe for its lifetime without increasing flood risk elsewhere.\n\nOverall, the proposal represents a modest and proportionate form of domestic development that respects the character of the area and neighbouring amenity.",
